"""
fake_claims.py — AquaFair
Owner: C

The full demo set as CLAIM dicts — 32 farms across four command areas.

⚠ DO NOT HAND-EDIT THESE NUMBERS.
They were GENERATED by running the real engine:

    from generate import demo_farms
    from farm_agent import build_claims
    from constants import WEATHER_STATES
    build_claims(demo_farms(), WEATHER_STATES["normal"])

An earlier hand-typed version drifted badly — paddy Ky was 1.25 when
constants said 1.35, and water volumes were 6-48% low because they had
been worked out at a 7-day cycle instead of 4. Every number on the
dashboard would have jumped at merge and looked like a rendering bug.

If constants.py or the demo spec changes, REGENERATE rather than patch.
Run `python3 fake_claims.py` — it compares itself against the live
engine and prints the correct values if they have drifted.

WHAT THIS IS FOR
The pipeline does not need it. app.py builds claims from demo_farms()
through farm_agent, so the live numbers are always the engine's own.
This file is a fixed reference for reading the CLAIM shape and for
tests that want stable input.

Rows are ordered HEAD TO TAIL within each source, matching
distance_from_head_m — the order impact.head_to_tail_split() serves
them in, so the current-practice baseline can be read straight off
this file.

Rows are ordered HEAD TO TAIL within each source, matching
distance_from_head_m — the order impact.head_to_tail_split() serves
them in, so the current-practice baseline reads straight off this file.

⚠ NEVER ALLOCATE ACROSS THE WHOLE LIST.
Farms belong to one tank or canal and never compete across them —
Tank A's water does not reach Tank B's farms, and no WUA has the
authority to move it. Use CLAIMS_BY_SOURCE, or filter on source_id.
Pooling all 32 would also silently invert the impact comparison,
because a canal's sugarcane would outbid a village tank's ragi.

F001-F004 (T01, Periya Eri) are the four farms the demo is rehearsed
on. The canal farms are much larger, which is what gives the Impact
panel a real smallholder-versus-large comparison.

Values are for the NORMAL scenario: ETo 5.0 mm/day, no rain, 4-day
cycle. Drought and rain produce different volumes.
"""

